{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517712-could-the-embrace-reverse-the-effects-of-aging","id":1517712,"title":"Could the embrace reverse the effects of aging?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-07-11T13:14:55-07:00","id":1517712,"title":"Could the embrace reverse the effects of aging?","content":"I don't remember if this is canon or fanon, but I've seen it said that the Beast may alter the body during the embrace in order to make it a better predator, including mending damage or even making cosmetic tweaks according to whatever set beauty standards to make them more alluring to prey (although I'm not sure the Beast would understand that concept). Assuming this is the case, could the protean/regenerative properties of the Embrace affect the damage that causes us to physically age in your opinion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 07-11-2023, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T15:35:56-07:00","id":1517716,"title":"","content":"The Beast altering the body is one of those concepts that gets mentioned in the fluff, but never gets a mechanical explanation. In the same vein as how low humanity/path vampires supposedly take on a more monstrous appearance.<br /> <br /> Many aspects of VtM are kept mechanically loose so that whatever head canon or concept you come up with can squeak by without too many issues. A good example is that while the Storyteller system allows you to spend XP to make changes to your character, it is never really explained how a Vampire was Appearance 1 at Embrace gets to be an Appearance 5 when they are supposed to be static in form for all time.<br /> <br /> But even the idea of being a better predator is a bad way of explaining the change because an Appearance 5 vampire who has only single dots in all mental traits won't survive for long, but we don't get fluff about all vampires getting an automatic IQ boost just from the embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-11T22:44:31-07:00","id":1517739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rhywbeth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517712-could-the-embrace-reverse-the-effects-of-aging#post1517712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">could the protean/regenerative properties of the Embrace affect the damage that causes us to physically age in your opinion?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think so<br /> There are plenty of very lethal Elders and Methuselahs &quot;trapped&quot; in the young body of a child basically<br /> The Settite <b>Neferu </b>is notable for her young Embrace (at or before the age of 14)<br /> <b>Ur-Shulgi</b> was described in Clan Novel: Assamite as &quot;Its naked, childlike body resembled a sculpture of hard-packed coal, each fissure, each crack in the kiln-hardened surface actually a jagged scar streaking like black lightning across the blackest midnight sky\u2014black except for a crescent and a handful of matching bone-white stars.&quot; and Beckett's Jyhad Diary desribed him &quot;In build, he looks like a young man, perhaps a teenager, but his skin is marked with orange-red veins the color of lava which give off a light that pulses in time with the music.&quot; - He looks like nothing so much as a scarred, burnt child, a young god born from fire and violence. His skin, obsidian-black with age, displays a lattice of scars, some of which weep blood when the methuselah becomes agitated. Here and there, bits of bone and sinew protrude from beneath his skin, as if its body has been flayed.<br /> <b>Nicolai Antonescu</b>, the former Tremere Primogen of Chicago was a \u2018Child\u2019 Elder, and <b>Halsey</b> in Swansong is a child.<br /> <b>Genina</b> a 6th generation Samedi is a little girl... and insane serial killer.<br /> <b>Christopher Houghton,</b> a 5th Generation Toreador elder and the first, and still most powerful vampire, in Los Angeles. while an Elder retained much of the aspects and inhibitions of a thirteen year old boy. As such, he is prone to act childish, forming crushes, and generally being unable to resist his urges.<br /> Velya the Vivisectionist, 5th Generation Tzimsice Embraced a 10 year-old girl, <b>Elaine Cassidy </b>as his &quot;bride&quot; after she systematically destroyed her family and she rode around grafted to his back... well becasue she became a Wight.<br /> Just to name a few<br /> <br /> There\u2019s a flaw one can tak that would mean that your character was Embraced as a child<br /> <br /> So I would say no, Embrace wont reverse aging, more like lock you in your age<br /> Nahum ben Enosh is a fourth generation vampire of clan Salubri was born in the early 150s CE and was Embraced 216 CE, bascially as a very old man (sorry for all those 60+ out there calling you very old)<br /> Francisco Domingo de Polonia's Embrace even &quot;trapped&quot; him in a body suffered a sunburn, to his chagrin, the sunburn that Polonia was suffering from at the time of his Embrace has stayed with him forever<br /> <br /> Embrace not even could &quot;fixed&quot; Polonia's skin... let alone Aging <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T02:45:50-07:00","id":1517748,"title":"","content":"As <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23890_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23890\" data-vbnamecard=\"23890\">Shadeprowler</a> said there\u2019s lots of examples of kindred frozen at young or elderly states at embrace so it dosen\u2019t generally rejuvenate (although a player could purchase merits to have this as a quirk of blood).<br /> <br /> Game wise however there are mechanics to show that the embrace over-rides or ignores your old human physiology such as the use of blood to boost attributes and the fact that you can play a 90 year neonate with a strength of 5 if you wish.<br /> <br /> So the predator efficiency is supported by by the lack of attribute caps for age (unless you take flaws) and blood boosting.<br /> <br /> Plus again nothing in the mechanics that says your character automatically takes a flaw to represent injuries you had in life, that\u2019s character background or flaws.<br /> There are a few canonical kindred embraced whilst dying on battlefields who don\u2019t bear the wounds they were dying from in undeath.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve always interpreted it as the beast is pretty unconcerned with physical appearance or beauty so it\u2019s static at embrace unless changed by external forces such as disciplines, rituals or aggravated damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27824-arcanus","name":"Arcanus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27824_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T03:25:25-07:00","id":1517752,"title":"","content":"I was primarily thinking of the damage of aging: thin, fragile skin that damages easily; weak joints and a spine bending under its own weight; failing sensory organs... The embrace typically repairs damage, flaws representing permanent injury seem to be outliers, so the embrace may affect the symptoms of age. Your skin thickens and firms into a better protective barrier, your spine straightens, your eyes clear again. You may still have white hair and some lines on your skin, but the overall effect would make you seem younger.<br /> <br /> Children don't really count, they've prevented from growing; ageing adults are going in the opposite direction and physically degenerating and becoming damaged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 07-12-2023, 06:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T04:33:12-07:00","id":1517754,"title":"","content":"Oh, those effects!<br /> Sorry, misunderstood<br /> But the answer for my part is still &quot;I think no&quot;<br /> But let me explain my reasons<br /> There are several elderly vampire who carreid their frail body in the undeath with them with rheumatic joinsts, aching back and arthritis, wrinkled, spoted skin, and bad eyesight sometimes the need of a hearing aid (and Flaws for these, etc.)<br /> Nahum ben Enosh needed a walking stick<br /> Louhi's appearance is that of an old witch, with the smell of several alchemical experiments and she always carries a black staff inscribed with various runes.<br /> Gunnhild, the &quot;Mother of Kings&quot; Fiend-witch, was in her seventies<br /> And of course there is Baba Yaga and her progeny Gutka, the Salt Queen\u200b<br /> Maureen O'Leary looked like a sweet little old lady. Often, a sweet little old lady in a wheelchair. - worth to mention tho, after her embrace she looked dead and when an old nurse bent over to check her pulse, Maureen sank her teeth into the matron's neck and drank. Within seconds, she felt her body growing stronger and the paralysis leaving her legs. Realizing freedom was at hand, she got out of bed and ran off into the night. This is interesting, since not the Embrace itself removed the paralisis, but the feeding.<br /> <br /> I think te <i>worst</i> infirmities of old age <i><b>won't matter as much</b></i> to a cainite.<br /> Even if arthritis and bad eyes follow them, and they had a mouth full of dentures, they'll likely develop retractable fangs anyway, and Disciplines/general blood buffing can overcome the rest as necessary.<br /> Similarly, their mind will no longer work on a neurological level, but instead on a supernatural, vitae-based one.<br /> Deteriorated muscles aren't following normal biology, it's all about efficient subconscious and intentional use of the blood. - witch would explain Maureen's recovery<br /> <br /> So I wouldn't say the Embrace reverse the effect, more like the usage of Vitae and Disciplines and the fact they are souls trapped in their own dead bodies, and &quot;not alive&quot; - the problems of the elders come from the fact their living bodies betraying them - negate most of the effects of aging... not the Embrace itself","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 07-12-2023, 08:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T08:26:27-07:00","id":1517778,"title":"","content":"I did this for an npc that was inspired in part by the notorious gunslinger Doc Holiday who was ravaged by his consumption disease. I kept his stamina and strength at 2 dots max as the embrace and a century plus of existence is not going undo the damage that his illness done to him and the potence &amp; fortitude disciplines can overcome the effects for a time. But I feel that even the magic of the vampire condition has it limits of what it can ease or undo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T13:04:56-07:00","id":1517809,"title":"","content":"There are various examples of vampires &quot;de-aging&quot;in media. What happens to Count Dracula after he arrives in England is only one example. Therefore, I wouldn't mind if this trope somehow enters play. The question is what is the best means to do so.<br /> <br /> It certainly shouldn't be free. There should be a cost. I would probably make it dependent on the vampire spending blood. Such &quot;de-aging&quot; only seems to happen after a vampire feeds a lot. Probably a fairly heavy cost in Blood Points, but once done the vampire &quot;resets&quot; to a particularly time period in their youth (probably limited to their prime adult years - somewhere in their late twenties to mid-thirties) for a certain amount of time - maybe a week or cycle of the moon.<br /> <br /> I would probably also require something else to be required. Maybe it requires a special Merit that is only available during character creation, or some level of Combination Discipline or advanced Discipline. It all depends on how exclusive you want this to be. Although this trope is used, we don't see it done all the time and I wouldn't all vampires doing it.<br /> <br /> But I would only have this be cosmetic (no improvements in any stats), and only temporary. Eventually the vampire would need to consume and burn large number of Blood Points again. There might also be some other cost that is more precious than just Blood Points, like permanent Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T13:34:49-07:00","id":1517816,"title":"","content":"I think it is connected to the origins of the vampire myth when a dead body would appear well fed after it bloated. In game, I have no problem with the embrace optimizing the body a bit towards an effective predator and thus shaving off maybe a few years when the newly embraced vampire was a bit beyond their prime - certain Clans and Bloodlines excluded.<br /> Any further than that would require sorcery or Discipline(s) imo. Fortitude and Vicissitude are good candidates, although I personally think that Vampires being locked in their body state after embrace is one of their defining characteristics that shouldn't be messed with too much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T15:00:48-07:00","id":1517831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517712-could-the-embrace-reverse-the-effects-of-aging?p=1517809#post1517809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are various examples of vampires &quot;de-aging&quot;in media. What happens to Count Dracula after he arrives in England is only one example. Therefore, I wouldn't mind if this trope somehow enters play. The question is what is the best means to do so.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, and this is related to another trope of vampires: that they steal things, including youth, as part of their Faustian bargain for immortality. I think when people talk about vampires being unchanging, they are focusing on one minor trope at the expense of more interesting tropes.<br /> <br /> Vampires are an entire pile of tropes, some of them clashing with other tropes. So you've got to pick some and discard others. I focus on vampires as beasts, and as Faustian bargainers. If this stasis stuff gets in the way of that to the slightest degree, bye-bye stasis trope. It's just not that important to me, especially in the context of a game that has experience points.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-12T22:45:31-07:00","id":1517861,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of a Flaw (probably 2 or 3 pts) where the vampire is however young they were at the Embrace when at max blood pool. But the lower their supply, the more aged they appear. Developing wrinkles, liver spots, dull eyes, and greying hair. Until they look almost cadaverous when their &quot;tank&quot; is near empty.<br /> <br /> I peg it at 2-3 pts, because it's a Flaw that won't affect the vampire too much in casual contact with strangers (unless the vampire spends a ton of blood points on the sly, whereby the shift in apparent age may be noticeable). But long term, it makes any attempt to maintain a mortal identity or even just long-term mortal relationships a dicey affair. Needing to keep one's BP topped off whenever interacting with certain mortals, to maintain the charade. Or having excuses for why you look more or less vibrant from encounter to encounter. (&quot;Yeah, I've been having a rough week. I need a spa date&quot; or &quot;I got Botox recently&quot;).<br /> <br /> On the other hand, some vampires with the Flaw might exploit it to maintain a duel identity (the classic &quot;here's my son, [Name] Junior; give him the same deference you would give me, as I've taught him everything I know&quot;). Though this means their &quot;old&quot; identity necessarily requires balancing on the knife's edge of hunger. Especially as the charade continues, and the vampire needs to go lower and lower to authentically fake natural aging.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-14T18:18:42-07:00","id":1517995,"title":"","content":"Yeah I've not heard of any case of a vampire being de-aged. The only time I've ever heard of a Kindred being de-aged was Anna Comnena who was Embraced when she was in her 70s and then having a Tzimisce fleshcraft body into a younger state. But that was because of Vicissitude, not the Embrace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-15T13:19:49-07:00","id":1518071,"title":"","content":"Also I seem to recall a 7th generation True Brujah elder who was embraced late in life in Cairo by Night and somehow and for some reason is looking younger and younger as time passes. Best guess it's something to do with this Temporis discipline that is reverting him to a younger form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-28T22:45:06-07:00","id":1519073,"title":"","content":"Vampires are creatures of the Weaver, ie stasis, more than they are of the Wyrm. This would imply that embracing a mortal will make them stay w/e age they were at the time of the embrace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24119-alucardtes","name":"Alucardtes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24119_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-29T21:43:03-07:00","id":1519154,"title":"","content":"If my memory still works, both Young and Old are flaws. And considering the Embrace, you'll change the age as much as a corpse. Of course, you can have a Claudia style vampire, or a Baba Yaga, but they're locked in their bodies, even if blood can be used to cure the worse of their handicaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27825-mrdrika","name":"MrDrika","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27825_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-08T16:26:07-07:00","id":1520160,"title":"","content":"I wonder if being a member of a much stronger generation would also undo the effects of the aging process or being ravaged by a terminal disease for more effectively then members of say like the 9th generation or higher? It's something that should be considered character creation in your own games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T19:08:04-07:00","id":1521716,"title":"","content":"Two schools of thought; vampires are frozen in time at the time of the embrace, or, the beast takes over and reverses the aging-process to its liking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"738"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-30T21:29:05-07:00","id":1521726,"title":"","content":"If vampires are frozen at the moment of the embrace, where do the fangs come from? Why don't all vampires have bite-marks on their throats? To me it is pretty obvious that the beast renovates its new home. Otherwise vampires would look more or less like zombies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-31T13:46:10-07:00","id":1521778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1517712-could-the-embrace-reverse-the-effects-of-aging?p=1521726#post1521726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If vampires are frozen at the moment of the embrace, where do the fangs come from? Why don't all vampires have bite-marks on their throats? To me it is pretty obvious that the beast renovates its new home. Otherwise vampires would look more or less like zombies.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is why if being part of a potent generation also would play bigger part in how the beast remakes it home was my main question. But as said this would be a house rule type of thing rather then anything official from the company.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-04T16:36:58-07:00","id":1522075,"title":"","content":"I would like to point out that Kindred as of V20 Dark Ages at the very least ARE changed or improved via the Embrace.<br /> <br /> The embrace literally is a rebirth via an ancient and terrible curse, a curse that is not entirely without benefit. Granted those benefits exist simply to make a better monster.<br /> <br /> We can see these changes if we look at a mortal characters character sheet and compare it to a vampire sheet.<br /> <br /> Mortals as base humans start with attributes of 6, 4, and 3. They begin play with abilities of 11, 7, and 4.<br /> <br /> Mr. Gone's character sheets for mortals show this. <a href=\"https://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/pdf/V20/V20_4-Page_Mortals_Interactive.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Masquerade 20th Aniversary Character Sheet (rocksolidshells.com)</a><br /> <br /> The Hunters hunted 2 which is for V20 also list human attributes as 6, 4, and 3 but hunters do possess more skills having the 13, 9, 5 spread like vampires. The players, for certain campaigns are also allowed to start with more experienced hunters with the vampire attribute pool of 7, 5, 3.<br /> <br /> In VTM 20 vampires begin play with attributes of 7, 5, and 3. They also start with abilities of 13, 9, and 5.<br /> <br /> <br /> This is an attribute and ability advantage above average mortals.<br /> <br /> <br /> There are also fluff pieces in v20 dark ages telling us how vampires are improved by the embrace.<br /> <br /> Take this excerpt from v20 dark ages as an example on page 22.<br /> <br /> &quot;I\u2019ve watched during the Embrace, watched<br /> as pox marks vanish and turn to baby-smooth skin, or<br /> even smoother. Once, I saw a lad who was struck by an<br /> affliction of the crown that left him bald as a friar, but<br /> didn\u2019t Damnation go and give him a head full of lovely<br /> hair. Didn\u2019t he just become a randy beast as a result? This<br /> is what I\u2019m saying! We\u2019re creatures made of sin rebuilt by<br /> the corruption of Caine to spread slowly but surely across<br /> all four corners of the earth.&quot;\u200b<br /> <br /> Now if this would effect age I do not know but regrowing hair, or fixing skin would make one look younger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27607-bloodyrelight","name":"BloodyRelight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27607_2.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}